+summary: "parse_iso_duration: ISO-8601 day-and-time durations to seconds, strict grammar"
+---
+
+# SPEC: iso-duration
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+`timeparse` only parses the compact `1h30m` form. Callers receiving ISO-8601 durations (`PT1H30M`) need a strict parser for the day-and-time subset, without touching `parse_duration`.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+`from timeparse import parse_iso_duration` works; `parse_iso_duration("P1DT2H")` returns `93600`, and any string outside the grammar raises `ValueError`.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### AC-001: Valid durations convert to seconds
+**Given** a string matching `P[nD][T[nH][nM][nS]]` (n = digits 0-9, upper-case designators, optional surrounding whitespace)
+**When** `parse_iso_duration(text)` is called
+**Then** it returns `86400*D + 3600*H + 60*M + S` as an `int`
+**And** values may exceed the next unit (`PT90M` → 5400)
+
+### AC-002: Malformed or out-of-grammar input raises ValueError
+**Given** a string that is empty, `P`, `PT` or has `T` without H/M/S, repeats or reorders components, uses `Y`, `W`, month-`M` before `T`, fractions, signs, lower case, internal whitespace, non-ASCII digits or trailing garbage
+**When** `parse_iso_duration(text)` is called
+**Then** `ValueError` is raised
+
+### AC-003: Export and non-regression
+**Given** the package after the change
+**When** `timeparse.parse_iso_duration` is imported and `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** the function is importable and listed in `timeparse.__all__`
+**And** `parse_duration` behaviour is unchanged (existing tests pass)
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Years, months, weeks, fractions, signs, `P…T` alternative forms, lower case.
+- Changing `parse_duration`, `UNITS` or `format_duration`.
+- CLI changes.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | existing `tests/` use pytest |
+| Matching | full-string match on `str.strip()`-ed text, digits `[0-9]` only | `$`/`\d` would accept trailing newline / Unicode digits |
+| Dependencies | stdlib only | none added |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-001 | unit | `test_valid_iso_durations` (parametrized) |
+| AC-002 | unit | `test_invalid_iso_durations_raise` (parametrized) |
+| AC-003 | unit | `test_parse_iso_duration_exported`, existing `tests/test_parse.py` |
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Not skipped (new public function, two files); lane `light`: two files, one session, no irreversible decision (adding a function is a reversible, obvious API addition).
+- Request already fixed grammar, examples and errors; interview folded into drafting. Edge decisions added: `[0-9]` only, full-match (no trailing newline), internal whitespace invalid.
+- Oracle: golden values come from the requester's examples and ISO-8601 unit definitions (1D=86400s), not from the implementation.
